---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Metered Commit Gates: Energy-to-Correct-Completion for Agentic Systems"
  description="About: Metered Commit Gates: Energy-to-Correct-Completion for Agentic Systems. Research paper in the OpenIE research catalog."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research paper · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Metered Commit Gates: Energy-to-Correct-Completion for Agentic Systems
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This paper joins Notational Intelligence and Mixture of Limits. Part I is the commit gate: a proposal may not authorize itself, an irreversible act runs only behind a certificate, and every decision is written to a receipt. Part II is the cascade: Lookup, then Formula, then Solver, then Model, stopping when the task completion predicate holds.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
      Systems are ranked by the joules needed to reach a correct completion. On an AMD Kria KV260 the onboard INA260 read 11,428 pJ per gate cycle (standard error 129 pJ, N = 4) for the WCA gate fabric, board level, not core rail. Other energy figures are analytical estimates.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion-laws">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion papers</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Research papers: <a href="/papers/agency/" class="text-brand-cyan">Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/gates/" class="text-brand-cyan">Metered Commit Gates</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="text-brand-cyan">Task Satiation vs. Aggregate Rebound</a>.
        Essay: <a href="/papers/spellcheck/" class="text-brand-cyan">Spell Check is Global</a>.
        Product white papers, kept apart: <a href="/products/mei/" class="text-brand-cyan">Metabolic Intelligence</a> · <a href="/products/jouleos/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Search for JouleOS</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Earlier addresses</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">/papers/ni/ and /papers/mol/ now open the matching part of this paper, section anchors included. /pdfs/ni.pdf and /pdfs/mol.pdf hold the merged PDF.</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">The cascade runs across the OpenIE family: <a href="https://stack.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">stack</a>, <a href="https://compute.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">compute</a>, <a href="https://knowledge.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">knowledge</a>, <a href="https://synthesis.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">synthesis</a>. The product path for the cascade is <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/mixture-of-limits" class="text-brand-cyan">openIE-dev/mixture-of-limits</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/gates/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/gates/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/gates.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/living/ni/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Interactive figures
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
